a, b, a_r, b_r and y are unsigned(7 downto 0) signals initialised to 0 (VHDL-2008, ieee.std_logic_1164 and ieee.numeric_std). The pairs (a, b) = (1, 2), (3, 4), (5, 6) and (7, 8) are applied before rising edges 1, 2, 3 and 4 respectively. What is y just after the 3rd rising edge?

process (clk)
begin
  if rising_edge(clk) then
    a_r <= a;
    b_r <= b;
    y   <= a_r + b_r;
  end if;
end process;

Two versions of y = (a + b) × c are written with all signals assigned inside if rising_edge(clk) then ... end if; (VHDL-2008, ieee.std_logic_1164 and ieee.numeric_std). The adder takes 3 ns, the multiplier 7 ns, and every register adds 1 ns (clock-to-Q plus setup); there is no skew. What are the maximum clock frequencies of A and B, and their latencies in clock cycles from the inputs a, b, c to y?

-- A
a_r <= a;  b_r <= b;  c_r <= c;
y   <= (a_r + b_r) * c_r;

-- B
a_r <= a;  b_r <= b;  c_r <= c;
s   <= a_r + b_r;  c_d <= c_r;
y   <= s * c_d;

The pipeline below stalls when en = '0' (VHDL-2008, ieee.std_logic_1164 and ieee.numeric_std; din, r1 and r2 are unsigned(7 downto 0) initialised to 0). Before rising edges 1 to 5, din = 11, 22, 33, 44, 55 and en = '1', '1', '0', '1', '1' respectively. What is r2 just after the 5th rising edge?

if rising_edge(clk) then
  if en = '1' then
    r1 <= din;
    r2 <= r1;
  end if;
end if;

The 2-register pipeline below has a synchronous reset (VHDL-2008, ieee.std_logic_1164 and ieee.numeric_std; all data are unsigned(7 downto 0) initialised to 0). Before rising edges 1 to 5, din = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and rst is '1' only before edge 3. What is r2 just after edges 4 and 5?

if rising_edge(clk) then
  if rst = '1' then
    r1 <= (others => '0');
    r2 <= (others => '0');
  else
    r1 <= din;
    r2 <= r1;
  end if;
end if;

The architecture below is instantiated with generic map (N => 6) (VHDL-2008, ieee.std_logic_1164 and ieee.numeric_std; sr starts at all zeros). din changes before a rising edge and then holds. Counting that edge as the first, after how many rising edges does dout show the new value, and how many flip-flops does the delay line contain?

type arr_t is array (0 to N - 1) of unsigned(7 downto 0);
signal sr : arr_t := (others => (others => '0'));
...
process (clk)
begin
  if rising_edge(clk) then
    sr <= din & sr(0 to N - 2);
  end if;
end process;
dout <= sr(N - 1);

A 16-bit adder is split over two pipeline stages: stage 1 adds the low bytes and keeps the carry, stage 2 adds the high bytes (VHDL-2008, ieee.std_logic_1164 and ieee.numeric_std; a, b and y are unsigned(15 downto 0), lo is unsigned(8 downto 0), ah and bh are unsigned(7 downto 0), all initialised to 0). a = x"12FF", b = x"0101" are applied before rising edge 1, and a = x"0001", b = x"0001" before edge 2. What is y just after edge 2?

if rising_edge(clk) then
  lo <= resize(a(7 downto 0), 9) + b(7 downto 0);
  ah <= a(15 downto 8);
  bh <= b(15 downto 8);
  y  <= (ah + bh + lo(8 downto 8)) & lo(7 downto 0);
end if;

The entity below models a 3-input FPGA look-up table (VHDL-2008, ieee.std_logic_1164 and ieee.numeric_std). With INIT = x"E8", which function of i(2), i(1) and i(0) does it implement?

entity lut3 is
  generic (INIT : std_logic_vector(7 downto 0) := x"E8");
  port (i : in std_logic_vector(2 downto 0); y : out std_logic);
end entity;
architecture rtl of lut3 is
begin
  y <= INIT(to_integer(unsigned(i)));
end architecture;
